<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-18403] Add ldlm.namespaces.*.enable_dynamic_lru parameter</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18403</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Originally, LDLM always had a static LRU size defined by the &lt;tt&gt;lru_size&lt;/tt&gt; parameter. When dynamic LRU sizing was implemented, setting "lru_size=0" was taken as "change to dynamic LRU sizing". &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For historic reasons, reading from the &lt;tt&gt;ldlm.namespaces.&amp;#42;.lru_size&lt;/tt&gt; parameter returns the number of locks currently in the LRU for that lock namespace. This usage to fetch the current lock count was replaced long ago by the "&lt;tt&gt;...lock_count&lt;/tt&gt;" parameter (similar to the "resource_count parameter, unless there are multiple DLM locks on a single object (eg. read locks, non-overlapping write locks, etc.).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Any usage of "&lt;tt&gt;lru_size&lt;/tt&gt;" in the test scripts to get the current lock count should be replaced by "&lt;tt&gt;lock_count&lt;/tt&gt;".  A second patch should be made to return the actual setting of &lt;tt&gt;lru_size&lt;/tt&gt; (including zero), not the current lock count in case of dynamic LRU size. &lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment />
